[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://systems/item_data.gd" id="1_item"]

[resource]
script = ExtResource("1_item")
id = "book_ilse_notebook"
display_name = "Ilse's Notebook"
description = "A small notebook with a burnt corner, stamped inside the cover with a lantern. The handwriting is a hedge-witch's; the stamp is the Order's."
value = 10
weight = 0.5
book_text = "Inside the cover, in a stranger's hand: \"Taken from the witch Ilse Marrow at her burning. For the Order's study. - H.\"

The rest is in a smaller, quicker hand.

Glamour is not a lie. A lie asks the other person to believe something false. Glamour shows them what they already half-believe, and lets them finish the thought themselves. That is why it works on frightened people best.

The wolves know me now. I leave them bones; they leave me alone. A fair trade, which is more than the garrison offers.

Zora asked me today why we hide. I told her: because the Order has never once burned the wrong person, if you ask the Order.

The lights at the stone circle sing at night. Not words. Something like words. I have written down what I can.

If you are reading this, I suppose they found me. Zora, if it's you: keep the window facing north. And stop apologising to the trees; they don't mind."
